},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing. Python and Java accept the same parameters on their SmartCard backends and likewise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignore them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a limitation of the application, not of SmartCard: an application that defines a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continuation on top of APDUs can report progress and be cancelled over the same transport."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CTAP2 does exactly that — it answers "},{"code":"0x9100","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the host polls with "},{"code":"NFCCTAP_GETRESPONSE","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is how "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Status\/waitingForUser(cancel:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" works over NFC. YubiOTP defines no such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exchange."}]}],"name":"Important"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Requires "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Feature\/challengeResponse","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", available on YubiKey 2.2 or later."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Performs an HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response against a slot.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"YubiKit","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"calculateHMACS